            "review_text": "Frick Teung\nPhnom Penh, Cambodia125 contributions\n0\nA Japanese restaurant full of charm and flavor\nApr 2017 • Friends\nWe were famished and I wanted our first meal in Saigon to be Japanese. I wanted to try a Japanese restaurant parallel to the street where our hotel was but it was unfortunately full with a waiting time of at least 30 minutes. Lo and behold, my friend caught sight of another Japanese place just across and we decided to go for it after checking the menu. \n\nThe place had a lot of Doraemon and other anime figurines. But besides that charm, the food we ordered were amazingly good - from the chicken karaage to ebi tempura to even the mixed vegetables.\n\nWe were too hungry and in praise to take pictures... Hahaha.\nRead more\nWritten April 15, 2017",
